<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/36/eng@/~cl_11__para_c> <https://schema.org/text> "by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsection: \" (3) Notwithstanding the provisions of subsection (2), a prescribed security which is deposited by a depositor with the central depository shall be capable of being utilised to settle a transaction which took place on a stock market of a stock exchange prior to the date of deposit of that prescribed security if the issuer registers the transfer of the security underlying such scrip in the name of the central depository or its nominee company and delivers the appropriate certificate to the central depository before the date for settlement of the transaction in accordance with the rules of the stock exchange.\"."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/36/eng@> .
